  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Desk Study - Iyendwe Valley Hydropower Plant, through CORE International, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $5,000 desk study reviewed a proposal for a feasibility study to evaluate the technical, financial, environmental, and other critical aspects of implementing a 15 megawatt (MW) hydropower plant in Zambias Northern Province. Currently, no sizable electricity generation facility exists in the Northern Province; the only electricity is supplied through a high voltage transmission line from southern Zambia, which is not sufficient to meet current electricity demand and is subject to low voltages and interruptions. The proposed hydropower plant would provide a dependable electricity supply, as well as significant developmental benefits and opportunities for U.S. exports.</narrative>
  </description>
